# Milestone 008: gRPC Entities Accounting & Sync - COMPLETED

## Date: 2026-03-01

## Summary
Implemented the distributed accounting engine that transitions DRL from passive
gRPC receiver to an active distributed accounting system.

## What was implemented

### Step 1: Protobuf Tooling
- Added `protoc` v29.6 to `mise.toml`
- Created `ci/scripts/proto-gen.sh` for code generation
- Added `mise run proto-gen` task

### Step 2: Protobuf Schema
- Created `internal/proto/accounting.proto` with CounterBatch/CounterEntry messages
- Generated `internal/proto/accounting.pb.go`

### Step 3: Accounting Configuration
- Added `AccountingConfig` and `AccountingRule` types to `internal/config/config.go`
- Implemented custom KDL `UnmarshalKDL` for parsing accounting rules
- Added `WindowDuration()` helper
- Added validation for rules (path prefix, limit, per)
- Updated `default.kdl` with empty accounting block
- Updated `deployments/drl/config.kdl` with sample rules
- Added config tests for KDL parsing and validation

### Step 4: Accounting Metrics
- Added 4 Prometheus counters: local_increments, remote_increments, flush, udp_recv
- Added helper methods: IncAccountingLocal/Remote/Flush/UDPRecv
- Updated metrics tests

### Step 5: UDP Counter Flusher
- Created `internal/accounting/flusher.go` with UDP batching protocol
- Enqueue/flush/receive loop with configurable interval and batch size
- sync.Pool for protobuf object reuse
- 6 tests covering enqueue, flush, receive, batch limits, lifecycle, protobuf roundtrip

### Step 6: Accounting Engine
- Created `internal/accounting/engine.go` with rule matching and entity tracking
- Process() matches rules, builds entities, determines ownership, increments locally or enqueues remotely
- 8 tests covering rule matching, local/remote processing, header filtering, stats

### Step 7: gRPC Server Integration
- Added `AccountingEngine` interface to `internal/grpc/server.go`
- Fire-and-forget `go s.engine.Process()` in Check() handler
- Added TestCheck_WithEngine test

### Step 8: Accounting Stats API
- Added `AccountingStatsProvider` interface to `internal/api/api.go`
- Created `GET /accounting/stats` endpoint (auth protected)
- Returns local_node_id, monitored_entities_count, batched_updates_pending
- 3 tests: unauthorized, with provider, nil provider

### Step 9: Main.go Wiring
- Creates Flusher and Engine when accounting rules are configured
- Passes engine to gRPC server and API server
- Flusher.Stop() in shutdown sequence

## Test Results
- All 257 tests pass
- All packages lint clean
- Coverage: accounting 86.1%, api 94.5%, config 92.2%, grpc 90.0%, metrics 97.5%

